---
wide: true
title: Try it
lead: The full editor in one tag, with every view. Edit the bitmark, or any view that edits back (JSON, HTML, XML).
---
<div class="demo">
  <div class="demo-bar">
    <span><code>&lt;bitmark-editor panes="json,html,xml,text,info,mappings"&gt;</code></span>
    <span>/bundled · parser {{ site.parserVersion }}</span>
  </div>
  <bitmark-editor class="demo-stage demo-tall" theme="auto" panes="json,html,xml,text,info,mappings" value="[.article]
# A short example
Hello **World**! This is ==highlighted==|highlight| text.

[.cloze]
The capital of France is [_Paris].

[.multiple-choice-1]
Which planet is the largest?
[-Mars]
[+Jupiter]
[-Venus]"></bitmark-editor>
</div>

<p>
  Things to try: type <code>[.</code> on a new line for bit types (Enter inserts the bit's template); hover a bit
  type; break the bitmark to see an error; edit the JSON and watch the bitmark follow. The views keep the same bit
  in view as you scroll.
</p>

<h2>The markup</h2>
{% highlight "html" %}
<bitmark-editor theme="auto" panes="json,html,xml,text,info,mappings" value="…" style="height: 520px"></bitmark-editor>
<script type="module" src="{{ site.cdn }}"></script>
{% endhighlight %}

<p>
  For your own layout, use <code>&lt;bitmark-session&gt;</code> and its panes instead:
  <a href="/guides/elements/">Custom elements</a>.
</p>

<script type="module" src="/bundled/bundled.js"></script>
